<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Rif Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1921 CE – 1926 CE · capital Ajdir</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Abd el-Krim's Berber republic in northern Morocco, which crushed a Spanish army at Annual and inspired anticolonial movements worldwide.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-el-krim">Muhammad ibn Abd el-Krim al-Khattabi</a>, a Rifian judge and journalist, united the tribes of the Rif against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-protectorate-in-morocco">Spanish protectorate in Morocco</a>. In July 1921 his forces destroyed a Spanish army at Annual, killing thousands. He proclaimed a republic with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajdir">Ajdir</a>, formally constituted in 1923.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic had ministries, a national assembly of tribal representatives, taxes and a disciplined army that used captured artillery and trench warfare. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-el-krim">Abd el-Krim</a> banned feuds and enforced Islamic law, aiming at a modern state. In 1925 his offensive against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-in-morocco">French protectorate in Morocco</a> brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> into the war.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>A combined Franco-Spanish force of hundreds of thousands, with a landing at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alhucemas-landing">Alhucemas</a> in 1925 and Spanish use of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chemical-weapons">chemical weapons</a>, overwhelmed the Rif. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-el-krim">Abd el-Krim</a> surrendered in May 1926 and was exiled to Réunion.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/rif-republic.jpg" alt="Rif Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Mysid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Republic_of_the_Rif.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1921 CE – 1926 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ajdir</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd el-Krim</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Riffian Berber, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of the Rif, Confederal Republic of the Tribes of the Rif</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1924&amp;focus=rif-republic" aria-label="Rif Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4581 905 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Rif Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4901 1161L4864 1148"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4864 1148h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4901 1161h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4901 1161h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ajdir. <a href="/atlas?year=1924&amp;focus=rif-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
